// csARM vphysics stub — round 25 (GENERATED by scripts/gen_vphysics_stub.py).
//
// The 2019 partner tree has no vphysics implementation (the IVP physics core
// never leaked).  The boot wall (run #160): CModelLoader::Init ->
// CollisionBSPData_LinkPhysics -> g_AppSystemFactory("VPhysicsCollision007")
// -> MISS -> Sys_Error "CollisionBSPData_PreLoad: Can't link physics";
// CPhysicsHook::Init also hard-fails without all three interfaces, and
// CPhysicsHook::LevelInitPreEntity dereferences physenv unconditionally
// right after physics->CreateEnvironment().
//
// This file ships no-op shells for the whole vphysics surface the boot /
// map-load / entity-spawn path touches.  All pure virtuals are emitted
// VERBATIM from the real 2019 header (vtable slot layout is therefore
// compiler-verified).  Environment/object creation returns live no-op
// singletons so the game treats "physics is running" and the map-load
// probe can go as deep as possible without a real IVP core.
//
// Interface names answered by CreateInterface / QueryInterface:
//   VPhysics031, VPhysicsSurfaceProps001, VPhysicsCollision007
//   (public/interfaces/interfaces.h:282 + vphysics_interface.h:134,1045)
